Subject: [PATCH 03/11] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20flick-to-throw=20=E2=80=94=20flin?=
 =?UTF-8?q?g=20a=20touch-dragged=20window=20to=20the=20adjacent=20display?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Releasing a single-finger window move with enough velocity throws the
window to the neighbouring output in the flick direction. Touch-only:
mouse moves are unaffected (they already relocate across the bezel when
the cursor crosses). Works for both Mod+touch and titlebar/xdg_toplevel
moves, which share MoveGrab's single touch-up handler.

- niri-config: flick-to-monitor (default on) + flick-velocity-threshold
  (default 800 px/s) knobs under touchscreen { gestures { } }, with
  accessors and parse tests.
- move_grab: per-axis SwipeTracker fed from touch motion; on release,
  retarget the in-flight interactive move to the adjacent output's centre
  (output_{left,right,up,down}_of) so interactive_move_end drops it there.
- docs: "Flick to Throw" section in Gestures.md plus the two knobs in
  Configuration:-Input.md and resources/default-config.kdl (and fills the
  swipe-multi-finger-scale gap in Gestures.md).

Fires only in the Move gesture state: floating windows throw in all four
directions; a tiled window throws once it has been picked up into a move
(a purely sideways drag on a tiled window stays column navigation — the
view-offset state — and is left untouched).

